From: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Sep 2024 15:32:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: skip secondary WED without primary

Do not attach a secondary HIF when the primary WED device is inactive.
The primary attach is attempted first, so its active state is a per-device
record of success that does not affect later mt7996-family devices or an
already configured alternative offload backend.

This avoids the call trace fixed by MediaTek's prerequisite patch without
turning a single device's attach failure into module-wide policy.

Adapted from MediaTek's 25.12 patch "Fix call trace happened when wed
attach fail".

Link: https://github.com/mediatek/mtk-openwrt-feeds/blob/671c2416d6219beb19abbb05709e418a6363be62/autobuild/unified/filogic/mac80211/25.12/files/package/kernel/mt76/patches/0040-mtk-mt76-mt7996-Fix-call-trace-happened-when-wed-att.patch
Signed-off-by: Rex Lu <rex.lu@mediatek.com>
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Paul-Louis Charrière <plcharriere@gmail.com>
---
Index: mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mmio.c
===================================================================
--- mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791.orig/mt7996/mmio.c
+++ mt76-2026.09.01~be5ce791/mt7996/mmio.c
@@ -508,6 +508,9 @@ int mt7996_mmio_wed_init(struct mt7996_d
 	if (!wed_enable)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (hif2 && !mtk_wed_device_active(wed))
+		return 0;
+
 	if (hif2)
 		wed = &dev->mt76.mmio.wed_hif2;
 
